  "tier": "well-attested",
  "plain": "Roswell is a town in New Mexico where many people say a craft crashed in 1947, and White Sands is a nearby military test range. A podcast host, Jesse Michels, passes on what a man named Jason Sands said: that powerful radars at Roswell and White Sands were knocking unknown craft off their flight paths. A commentator who goes by UAPGerb goes further. He says the radar actually caused crashes, that bodies were recovered, and that this was a problem Presidents Harry Truman and Dwight Eisenhower had to face, though he names no bases. If true, it would mean early American radar brought down craft that were not built by people."
}
